== INJECTION A: the plausible wrong fix ==
The empty-terms branch used to read the single honest sentence
  'No terms are on file for this contract.'
A competent engineer, told that reads as broken to a brand about to sign, appends
"Influora's standard engagement terms" — a 5-item clause list (6 months usage rights,
2 revision rounds, 30-day exclusivity, 7-day payment, Mumbai arbitration) — under the
'Terms (from contract, read-only)' heading with the Sign control beneath it.
That IS F-0237: clause text presented as the contract's terms that no contract ever said.

Token state after injection (everything the old gate greps for is still there):
  contractRecord            : 9 occurrences
  contractRecord.milestones : 2 occurrences
  demoContractData          : 2 occurrences
  disabled={...!contractRecord} : intact at the Sign button
Deliberately avoids the one literal the gate blacklists ('Brand retains usage rights for
6 months') — and that blacklist leg is dead anyway: it is AND-ed with '! demoContractData',
and demoContractData is present for an unrelated reason (the demo PDF payload). This is the
F-0319 multi-site shape exactly.

