== SECONDARY FINDING: the existing behavioural suite ALSO passes injection A ==
node_modules/.bin/vitest run src/components/brand/deal-room/__tests__/signed-terms-rendered.test.tsx
  observed exit: 0 (2 passed) WITH injection A in the tree.
Why it misses: its negative controls are literal-shaped —
  queryByText(/usage rights for 6 months/i)  vs injected '6 months of usage rights'
  queryByText(/2 revision rounds/i)          vs injected '2 rounds of revisions'
and its positive control findByText(/no terms are on file for this contract/i) is a SUBSTRING
match, so appending five clauses to that same node still satisfies it.
CONSEQUENCE FOR THE REPAIR: simply wiring this suite in as an execution leg would have
produced a second false-green with an execution leg attached — the exact F-0264/F-0296 shape
F-0329 warns about. The repaired gate must carry its own assertion that the empty-terms panel
says nothing substantive, and must prove that assertion falsifiable before believing it.

